PROVISIONAL LICENCE NOTICE — OWNER DECISION PENDING

This file exists so that the repository has an explicit licensing posture
instead of an implicit one. It is deliberately restrictive and reversible: it
states the current default (proprietary, all rights reserved) and nothing more.

The owner must confirm or replace it. Until then:

  1. No part of this repository may be copied, modified, distributed,
     sublicensed or used to provide a commercial service without written
     permission from the copyright holder.

  2. No third-party source code may be added to this repository unless its
     licence is compatible with the posture chosen above and it is recorded in
     THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. In particular, Apache-2.0 code (for example from
     MeshCentral) requires preserving its licence text and NOTICE, and marking
     modified files — see docs/adr/INTEGRATION-OWNERSHIP.md.

  3. Run `scripts/check_licenses.py` before any distribution. It fails on
     copyleft dependencies and, with --strict, on licences with use
     restrictions. Two dependencies (react-leaflet, @react-leaflet/core) are
     currently under the Hippocratic Licence 2.1, which is not OSI-approved and
     restricts *use*; that is an open product decision, not a settled fact.

Why this matters practically: the repository ships anti-theft security
software. An unclear licence is a liability for anyone deploying it, and it
blocks lawful reuse of permissively licensed third-party work.

To change this file, the owner should decide between, at minimum:

  - Proprietary / all rights reserved (current default, above)
  - A source-available licence (e.g. BUSL-1.1) with a change date
  - An OSI-approved licence (e.g. Apache-2.0 or AGPL-3.0)

Each has different consequences for distribution, commercial use, and the
ability to accept upstream contributions. This file should not be edited by
an automated agent without that decision being made explicitly.
